TYPE=u32
GROUP=batch
DOC=SPIRA_BATCH_MAXPAR — A small single-box install: at most eight suites at once (0 is still refused).
SCHEMA=testenv's own suite concurrency cap (testenv/DESIGN.md §4.3, `schedule::maxpar`). Unset derives a quarter of the CPU ceiling, clamped to [2, 16] — never the hardware bound. 0 and anything that doesn't parse are refused outright, not read as "unlimited" (sp-tj8k3: a batch_maxpar of 0 in production put 61 containers and load 90 on one host).
DEFAULT<<'SPIRA_CONF_DEFAULT_EOF'
    # Registered default (sp-kuwp6s, per Ryan 2026-10-07): A small single-box install: at most eight suites at once (0 is still refused).
    : "${SPIRA_BATCH_MAXPAR:=8}"
SPIRA_CONF_DEFAULT_EOF
